MASTER REFERENCE SPECIFICATION
Standing Instructions
Literal scale • adult anatomy • physical realism • continuous scene logic
Controlling principle
Shrink the person, not the world. Every dimension, body proportion, physical contact, camera view, and panel transition must remain believable in a full-scale 1:1 environment.


Purpose  This document consolidates the standing creative requirements for writing and evaluating shrinking-scene prompts. It favors exact measurements, explicit continuity, adult biological fidelity, credible physics, and natural human behavior over visual shortcuts or ambiguity.
Rule priority  The non-negotiable locks govern all later sections. If a lower-level preference conflicts with a lock, the lock wins. The previously drafted six-round interrogation set remains advisory unless it is separately confirmed as a standing rule.


