13. Consolidated exclusion register
The following terms identify visual or narrative failure modes. They are constraints against the result, not elements to depict.
Category
Excluded outcomes
Scale and continuity
wrong inches; wrong centimeters; incorrect sizes; size drift; fluctuating scale; random shrinking or growth; mid-height transition; false comparison; rescaled environment; shrunk furnishings; perspective mismatch; continuity reset
Anatomy and proportion
stretched or shortened arms; elongated or stumpy limbs; oversized head; compressed torso; warped feet; uneven limb thickness; deformed or dislocated joints; hyperextension; broken-looking wrists; elastic, rubbery, boneless, or spaghetti limbs; elongated fingers; spider-like fingers; skewed proportions
Camera and perspective
forced perspective; fisheye; barrel distortion; extreme foreshortening; peripheral lens stretching; wide-angle body distortion; perspective elongation; warped torso; distorted limb scale; camera angle that changes factual size
Duplication and anatomy errors
duplicated humans; cloned faces; duplicate hands or arms; random off-screen body parts; unrequested people; detached shadows; extra panels; repeated scene beats
Support and physics
floating humans or objects; invisible or intangible support; missing contact shadow; absent compression; weightlessness; rigid water; phasing through solids; unsupported reach; effortless grasp
Synthetic appearance
