hallucinated detail; ambiguity; implausibility; random addition; blandness; laziness; recycled content; blowing raspberries unless explicitly requested


14. Advisory preflight checklist
This checklist is a practical review aid derived from the standing rules. It does not convert the earlier six-round interrogation set into a separate locked rule.
☐ Is the shrinking fully complete, with no intermediate body size or lingering effect?
☐ Is every shrunk person unmistakably the same adult, with mature anatomy and identity intact?
☐ Does one uniform scale factor govern the entire body?
☐ Is each exact size stated consistently in every place where drift could occur?
☐ Does every SI or customary-unit conversion calculate correctly?
☐ Has the world retained its ordinary full-scale dimensions?
☐ Could any object be mistaken for a miniature or conveniently resized substitute?
☐ Does the camera preserve factual size, adult proportions, and spatial relationships?
☐ Are foreshortened limbs still anatomically legible at their true length?
☐ Does each panel continue the same location, people, objects, lighting, and action state?
☐ Can every visible change be traced to a cause?
☐ Does every body and object have a visible, credible support?
☐ Do contacts show pressure, compression, fold, overlap, occlusion, or shadow as appropriate?
☐ Do hair, fabric, water, and loose objects respond to gravity and motion?
☐ Are expressions and gestures specific to what each person knows and feels?
☐ Are posture, hands, gaze, shoulders, pelvis, and limbs naturally asymmetric?
☐ Does every person appear exactly once, with no duplicate part, face, shadow, or extra figure?
☐ Does the rendering read as candid documentary photography rather than art, CGI, or a toy scene?
☐ Is the wording singular and explicit enough that a model cannot reasonably interpret it two ways?
☐ Does the final scene preserve all requested details without adding generic substitutions?
